 {:seon.task/name "a-diff-of-two-commits-costs-the-nodes-that-differ"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.ctx/moved` diffs two db values of one branch with ``datahike.api/datoms-diff`` on ``:eavt`` over the whole range; for two plain values Datahike walks both trees level by level (``datahike.index.persistent-set/diff``), skips every child whose address both sides hold (so it reads only the nodes that differ: the cold konserve reads equal the unshared nodes), then re-checks every candidate datom with a membership lookup on both whole sets. Measured 2026-11-11 (Deep fixes' helper, a fresh LMDB store of 250k eavt datoms, eavt height 4, bf 64; ticks exact, the same in three runs), per diff of two consecutive commits: 21 datoms at the eid tail 238k ticks warm, 389k on the first call in a process, 533k cold (14 konserve reads, 7 nodes a side, ~21k ticks a cold node); one upsert 212k warm; 23 scattered 1.05 M; 201 at the tail 1.04 M; 203 scattered 22.2 M warm (29.3 M cold), 18.9 M of it in ``java.util.HashSet`` ``retainAll``, which Jolt implements as a scan of its argument for each element (``reference-code/jolt/host/chez/java/host-static-classes.ss``, near line 1915): quadratic in the diff's size, a class in Jolt (any retainAll with a hashed argument), not only here. The floor: the transaction's own datoms (what `seon.ctx/moved` already takes when b is the tx's db-after) 2.9k ticks at 21; an address-skipping walk with no re-check about 15-20k warm. Four fixes, each measured on an instrumented copy that answers the same as datoms-diff (warm, 21 tail datoms unless said): (1) drop the membership re-check, since on Jolt no branch buffers edits and the unshared leaves' merge is the answer (upstream's port says the same): -58k, and -600k at 201 tail datoms; (2) the shared-address test with Clojure sets, as upstream's prune-shared, or Jolt's retainAll asking its argument's contains: -29k, and 21.9 M to 3.77 M at 203 scattered; (3) no in-range test when the bounds are the whole index: -32k; (4) the comparator called as a fn and vectors in the merge: -5.5k. Together 238k to 94k warm (2.5x) and 22.2 M to 2.26 M at 203 scattered (10x). Upstream's sorted-set port already has this shape (task ``org.replikativ.persistent-sorted-set/upstreams-diff-and-bulk-build-are-on-jolt``): adopting its diff and keeping Datahike's range bound is the 90/10. Not decided here: whether `advance`'s diffs could read a commit's own datoms instead (Context's call). Proof to write (named, not written): a cost proof of ``datahike.api/datoms-diff`` of two commits by the datoms that differ, at 1, 21 and 203 scattered datoms on a store on disk, linear in them. Owner: Deep fixes (Datahike, Jolt)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}
]
